          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.544,
            0.29,
            0.882,
            0.347
          ],
          "content": "(ii) The mirror is tilted, but the light ray still falls along the normal to the tilted surface."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.539,
            0.349,
            0.883,
            0.407
          ],
          "content": "(iii) The mirror is tilted, and the light ray falls at an angle of $2 \\bar { 0 } ^ { \\circ }$ from the normal."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.542,
            0.409,
            0.883,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": "Draw the reflected ray in each case (Use a ruler and protractor for accurate drawing). What is the angle of reflection in each case?"
